Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: You should not use prednisone if you are allergic to prednisone.
You should not use prednisone if you have a systemic fungal infection.
To make sure prednisone is safe for you, tell your doctor if you have or have ever had:
an infection of any kind, including tuberculosis, hepatitis B, herpes infection of the eye, or a fungal infection;
Diarrhea has no clear cause.
Time is spent in the tropics.
Prednisone can wake up a parasite infection.
The parasite infection is amebiasis.
The parasite infection is threadworm.
malaria, especially cerebral malaria (malaria affecting the brain);
liver disease, such as cirrhosis;
kidney disease;
heart disease, heart failure, high blood pressure or low potassium levels;
an underactive thyroid;
diabetes;
osteoporosis;
glaucoma or cataracts;
stomach ulcers, ulcerative colitis, diverticulitis, or a history of bleeding in the stomach or bowel;
myasthenia gravis (a condition that causes muscle weakness); or
depression, mood swings or another mental health condition.
Long-term steroid use can cause bone loss.
Your risk is higher if you smoke.
Triplet: ["prednisone", "can reactivate", "threadworm"]

The relation 'can reactivate' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug may cause the dormant or latent infection specified by the object entity to become active again.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'used after': The subject drug is used following the treatment or condition specified by the object entity.
B. 'has effect': The subject drug produces the effect specified by the object entity.
C. 'has onset of effect': The subject drug starts to work or shows its effect within the time period specified by the object entity.
D. 'may be used for': The subject drug may be used for the purpose or condition specified by the object entity.
E. 'has side effect': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect or symptom specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
